Imported: top-level C, headers and JavaScript, Makefile, VERSION, Changelog,
readme.txt, test262.conf, test262_errors.txt, tests/, examples/ and doc/.
Release tooling and the separately distributed Test262 corpus are not included.

Local changes:
- Native pcc/mk build using APE. Compiler adaptations include value constructors,
  uniform closure bitfields, flexible arrays, regexp stack fields, portable
  constants and a switch-based interpreter.
  On amd64, the build requires generated9's 6c unordered-comparison fix.
- Checked heap allocations replace alloca; stack and memory limits remain active.
- Plan 9 floating-point initialization and allocation accounting, environment
  updates and realpath are in plan9.[ch]. Negative zero, subnormal and nonfinite
  constants use their IEEE 754 representation to avoid 6c constant-folding errors.
- poll9.[ch] adapts the event loop to APE select; handler registration checks its
  descriptor limit. Workers, atomics and shared-library loading are disabled.
- Plan 9 terminal/stat/time adaptations in quickjs-libc.c; regression tests and
  build notes are local additions.
- examples/raytrace.js is a local, standalone PPM ray tracer.

Anand Tamariya's existing Plan 9 port was consulted:
