math/: double-precision routines and supporting tables from musl 1.2.5
https://musl.libc.org/
https://musl.libc.org/releases/musl-1.2.5.tar.gz
SHA-256: a9a118bbe84d8764da0ea0d28b3ab3fae8477fc7e4085d90102b8596fc7c75e4

Sources correspond to src/math/<filename>. The common libm.h is adapted from
src/internal/libm.h. Copyright and license information is retained in
math/COPYRIGHT and the individual source files, including the Arm, Sun and
FreeBSD notices. These routines supply C99 functions missing from APE and the
IEEE 754 domain, signed-zero and subnormal behavior JavaScript requires.

Local math changes: APE includes/types, portable union accessors in libm.h,
hexadecimal floating literals rewritten as round-trip decimal literals,
negative-zero literals and sign changes represented as bits, double operands
in mixed-precision expressions, and invalid operations expressed using runtime
values to avoid constant folding. No changes are made to APE itself.

New generated9 files and contributions use the repository's root LICENSE.
